# =====================================================================
#  tb_agu  --  unit test for agu.sv (Address Generation Unit)
# =====================================================================
#  Parameters    : ROWS=4  STORE_LATENCY=8
#                  ACT_BASE=20  OUT_BASE=100
# 
#  WHAT THE AGU DOES
#    w_addr    counts DOWN 3..0 during wload_phase.  The array's
#              vertical bus is a downward shift register while wload=1,
#              so the row fed FIRST travels furthest and lands in the
#              BOTTOM row.  Counting down is what puts weight row r
#              into array row r.
#    act_addr  counts UP from act_base during compute_phase.
#    out_we    is compute_phase pushed through a 8-deep shift register,
#              so the write strobe structurally meets its own data.
# 
#  Driven by testbench-generated phase enables, NOT the real controller,
#  so an FSM bug cannot mask an AGU bug.
# 
#  TEST PLAN
#    T8  reset leaves no stale strobes
#    T1  weight addresses count down 3..0, one per wload clock
#    T7  wload / valid_in / rd_en track their phase enables
#    T2  the weight counter re-arms between jobs
#    T3  activation addresses count up from act_base
#    T5  out_we/out_addr arrive exactly 8 cycles later
#    T6  exactly one write per vector: none extra, none missed
#    T4  a different act_base / out_base pair is honoured
# =====================================================================
